proposed_statement_changes.proposed:
Conditional on \((S_m,Z_{S_m})\), the fixed-baseline product law gives, for every local increment \(v\in\mathbb R^{r+s}\) for which \(\beta+v/\sqrt m\in\mathcal U\),
\[
\log\frac{dP_{\beta+v/\sqrt m}^{\mathcal O_m}}
{dP_{\beta}^{\mathcal O_m}}
=\sum_{i\in S_m}
\log\frac{p_{Z_i,\beta+v/\sqrt m}
(Y_{in}(Z_i)\mid x_{in})}
{p_{Z_i,\beta}(Y_{in}(Z_i)\mid x_{in})}.
\]
The conditional covariance of the associated central sequence is the random empirical information matrix
\[
\mathcal I_m(\beta;S_m,Z_{S_m})
=\frac1m\sum_{i\in S_m}
E_\beta\!left[s_{Z_i,\beta}s_{Z_i,\beta}^{\mathsf T}\mid x_{in}\right].
\]
The assumptions defining \(\mathfrak M\) do not imply \(\mathcal I_m(\beta;S_m,Z_{S_m})\to I(\beta)\), because they impose no continuity or empirical convergence condition on conditional score second moments as functions of the baseline.  Therefore those assumptions alone do not establish the advertised LAN-to-action transfer, the efficient upper bound, the arbitrary-action lower bound, or the exact Horvitz--Thompson curvature constant \(B(\beta)\).

